                    <ref target="frus1944v01#pg_863">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1944, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 863</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d84-f3" n="2" xml:id="d84-f3-content">
                <p>In reply, the Charge in China was informed in telegram 489, March 24, 7 p.m.,
                    that the Department was awaiting the Soviet Ambassador’s views regarding the
                    note transmitted to him March 17 with respect to the Chinese proposals. For text
                    of note, see telegram 619, March 16, 11 p.m., to Moscow, <ref target="#pg126">p.
                        126</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
